Z||000000||penetrator||10-29-1999||09:26 AM||||My car stalls when its hot and i stopping at streetlights. And it is not hard to restart efter but the rpm falls down directly to 700-800 rpm and the die again, its not fun to have to use one foot on both brake and throttle pedal. =(<P>I have cleand the IAC (as the fierostore said)  Checked all cables,EGR, pipes'n'stuff.<BR>I also checked so the clutch pedal did't short any cables under the dash.<BR>(and i need a speedometer gear, where can i get one of these ?, im from Sweden)<P>My Car is a Fiero 86 GT v6 4-speed manual.<P>Thanks<BR>Magnus||||reg||8
Z||000001||Thomas||10-29-1999||11:30 AM||||I fix the same Problem on the same car:<BR>At the Idle air controll solenoid you find a small hook. This hook stay in Zero (up) at idle. If you accelerate this hook is pressed down from the small metalplate lay over the hook. The hook is hold from a little screw.<BR>Try to press the hook in idle up with your finger. If its go up, then it is loose.<BR>Disconnect the cabel and build out the sensor<BR>in front of the screw. Be carefull at the two screws for the sensor, the are made with aluminium. Now you can fix the inner hook screw in idle position(hook must be in uper position). Reconnect all.||||reg||1
