Z||000005||theogre||10-29-1999||08:08 PM||||As far as I can tell, Thomas really means the TPS. Correct me if I'm wrong, but Fiero V6 IAC is an air bypass valve the same as it is on the 4cyl. I don't have my book handy.<P>To clarify...... The TH125c automatic has a history of problems with the clutch in the TC. It stalls at every traffic light when the TC lockup solinoid hangs keeping the TC locked.<P>A similar condition can happen to a stick car if the clutch is dragging. Of course this also causes the thing to shift like a turd.||||reg||1
