Z||000012||Thomas||11-10-1999||11:33 AM||||Hallo Eddie<BR>I´m from germany and i never learning english in school, only from news sides in sweden. ( a joke too) <BR>I learned my english by my self and by reading the Fiero Service Book and at my visit in LA,SF,Miami and Orlando.(and FOCOA too)<P>Hallo theogre<P>That´s right. I mean the TPS.<BR>Penatrator have a 4 speed manuel.<P>Hallo Penetrator<BR>I´ve got a Problem with the Pin at the clutchpedal some jears ago too.<BR>Change the pedal to a 87 pedal. They made with steel and not with aluminium, like in the 84 - 86 Fieros. At my car i put the Metal back on the pin. It works now some jears.<BR>And i can tell you what Problem you get in the next, the slave cylinder, the hydro line to the slave cylinder, the clutch fork, the clutch bearing, the pressure plate ....<P>I´ve got all this little problems in the last 7 jears---- I HATE THE CLUTCH %6%§4*#<P>In the moment my Goldy stay in my garage and waits for changing the clutch again.<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000013||penetrator||11-11-1999||12:01 AM||||Hi Tomas!<P>Okey, i'll check for a 87 clutch pedal.<P>But i already changed the preassure plate, disc and release bearing. It was after that we discovered the worn Pin on the pedal.<BR>My car has only 80 000 Kilometers on it. So i only had one clutch change. <P>Thanks<BR>Magnus||||reg||10
